{"text":"The defect has been located, fixed, and verified:\n\n**Defect:** In `src/paginate.js`, the `pageBounds` function computed the end offset as `Math.min(start + pageSize - 1, total)`, which is inclusive. This caused the boundary to be off by one — for example, on a complete page of 10 records (indices 0–9), it returned `{ start: 0, end: 9 }` instead of the expected exclusive-end `{ start: 0, end: 10 }`.\n\n**Fix:** Changed the expression from `start + pageSize - 1` to `start + pageSize`, making `end` an exclusive upper bound consistent with the test expectations and standard half-open interval semantics.\n\n**Verification:** All 2 tests pass:\n- ✔ uses an exclusive end offset on a partial final page\n- ✔ does not include a phantom record on a complete page","toolCalls":[],"finishReason":"stop"}